   ],
   "paragraph": "Building computers for AI creates two sides of a bill: large technology companies pay for capacity, while data centre operators earn money providing it. Think of a restaurant delaying an expansion: it keeps cash, but its builder loses expected work. After Democrats won both chambers of Congress, Microsoft, Amazon and Alphabet shares rose while several data centre operators fell. Reuters attributed the split to expectations that slower construction could ease big technology companies\u2019 spending while hurting operators and suppliers. Opposition in Texas and Georgia adds uncertainty. But these price moves reflect expectations about possible regulation, not evidence of newly enacted restrictions or cancelled projects.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "gpt-6.1-sol"
  },
  {
   "id": "cohere",
   "headline": "Cohere hosts rival models in private vaults",
   "facts": [
    "Nov3 third-party open models in dedicated Model Vault",
    "Zero data retention by default, vendor claim",
    "Encrypted tier protects processing and currently US-only",
    "Priced per GPU/hour; no independent audit in packet"
   ],
   "sources": [
    "https://cohere.com/blog/open-source-model-vault",
    "https://docs.cohere.com/v2/changelog/model-vault-open-models"
   ],
   "paragraph": "A company using an AI model sends it information and receives an answer. Cohere\u2019s Model Vault offers a private place to do that on dedicated computing infrastructure, now with other companies\u2019 open models alongside its own. Think of renting a separate kitchen rather than sharing the counter. By default, Cohere says it does not retain prompts or answers. Its Encrypted option adds confidential computing, protection for data while the computer processes it, which Cohere says prevents even the host or Cohere from seeing those exchanges. Those security claims lack independent confirmation in the available sources. Customers pay per GPU hour, and the Encrypted option is currently available only in the US.",
   "edited": "none",
   "explainer": "gpt-6.1-sol"
  }
