   "cycle": "The indicators suggest a highly indebted phase with less room for fiscal mistakes, rather than a dated prediction of crisis. Like a family devoting a large share of income to interest, refinancing costs constrain other choices. Debt relative to revenue increased over the year, while growth in foreign Treasury holdings slowed; the script\u2019s mixed-period ratios are rough gauges, not a clean national cash-flow account.",
   "asset_classes": "In the framework, positive real yields reward the purchasing power of cash and bonds and compete with gold. If financing pressure later forces easier money and currency dilution, that channel can favour gold; stocks depend on productivity and profits against financing costs. Today\u2019s reversal in the dollar does not prove that such a monetary transition has started. Unlike a debt crisis met with monetary easing, this case still has positive real yields competing with gold; the election result does not establish a shift to financing through newly created money."
